<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n10225" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀντιόομαι</span></b> , fut.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ώσομαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					7.9
				</span></i>
			.<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γ́,</span><i><span class="en">
				102
			</span></i>, al.: aor.
			
				Pass.
			
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἠντιώθην,</span>
			
				Ion.
			
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀντ-</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					4.126
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				7.9
			</span></i>.<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ά</span>, al.:—<i>resist,
				oppose,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					1.76
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Supp.</u>
				389
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινὶ ἐς μάχην</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					7.102
				</span></i>
			: abs., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἱ ἀντιούμενοι,</span>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἱ ἐναντίοι</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				1.207
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				4.1
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> in <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				9.7
			</span></i>.<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">β́</span> (dub.), c. acc., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸν Πέρσην ἀντιώσεσθαι ἐς τὴν
			Βοιωτίην</span> that ye <i>would meet</i> him in Boeotia.
				(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐναντ-</span> is used in pure 
				Att.
			, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ.</span> in <i><span class="en">
				Aen.Tact.
				36.7
			</span></i>. The Homeric forms <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀντιόω,
				ἀντιόωσι,</span> etc., belong to <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀντιάω.</span>)</div>
